	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Pololu D36V50F5 (item #4091) step-down regulator: 5V out, 5.5A typical at 36V in, input 5.5-50V, 1in square, 12-pin 2x6 header on 0.1in grid, three M2 mounting holes. VIN/GND/VOUT/VRP are duplicated across both rows to carry the current; EN and PG are single pins. VRP is reverse-protected VIN. Powers the logic domain from the M18 electronics pack (~21V, well inside range). PIN-1 ASSUMPTION: footprint pad 1 (the rectangular pad) is taken as Pololu's first pin, VIN - verify against the silkscreen. MOUNTING HOLES ARE NON-PLATED (np_thru_hole, 2.2mm, no annular ring) so an M2 screw or standoff cannot touch copper. KEEPOUT: pad 11 (EN) at (1.37, 16.93) is only ~4.4mm from the hole at (0, 21.10); EN is pulled up 100k to reverse-protected VIN, so any copper path from that hole to EN shuts the 5V rail off. Keep pours and washers clear of it.")
	(tags "Through hole socket strip THT 2x06 2.54mm double row")
